                        "form": "phantasies"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1512570e-843e-4b73-b5ec-fb29bfe08ac2",
                        "entry_id": "69dd2fe7-e527-3b52-acc0-292154e85079",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Phantasie"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee2c7740-d03d-318e-bffe-f7a97a91f8ea",
                        "entry_id": "69dd2fe7-e527-3b52-acc0-292154e85079",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Psychique imaginaire qui a la structure d'un scénario soutenant la réalisation d'un désir."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc246e3b-1fc2-36ed-99ad-8599576511cc",
                        "entry_id": "69dd2fe7-e527-3b52-acc0-292154e85079",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Capacité à se visualiser mentalement des choses sans les avoir devant soi."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "57015ac6-993f-4c64-a4a3-ff8fced0d11f",
                        "source_entry_id": "69dd2fe7-e527-3b52-acc0-292154e85079",
                        "source_sense_description": "Psychique imaginaire qui a la structure d'un scénario soutenant la réalisation d'un désir",
                        "target_lang_word": "phantasia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "phantasia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "075fcc7d-d421-35ce-8bb1-7f6993232f53",
                                        "entry_id": "de09c59b-8d55-3c20-a3eb-5b9a9c76216e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something imaginary; a fantasy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca91cd04-1339-47d3-95c2-caebb006f683",
                                                "sense_id": "075fcc7d-d421-35ce-8bb1-7f6993232f53",
                                                "text": "But even here suppuration does not always stop, reaching often the fore-arm, and in such cases even life is endangered. Unhealthy granulations, thrombosis of veins, septicæmia and pyæmia cause death. This picture is not merely a phantasia, but exists in reality, and I myself had occasion to witness two cases of this kind in the surgical wards of Berlin; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14ca6b73-c08b-4339-9f86-1af1e6c69736",
                                                "sense_id": "075fcc7d-d421-35ce-8bb1-7f6993232f53",
                                                "text": "When one thing fits into another, when all the parts mutually support and are supported, when a theory is capable of accounting for all questions, and thus is, in a certain sense, self-balanced and self-sustained and entire, we have a phantasia of truth forced upon our minds, even against our will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e826060b-dc98-4c0f-9225-1c00360530d2",
                                                "sense_id": "075fcc7d-d421-35ce-8bb1-7f6993232f53",
                                                "text": "What we consider a clear logical conclusive chain of argument is as often a phantasia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "870a5eab-2d75-391d-9a6a-07349ad8cec6",
                                        "entry_id": "de09c59b-8d55-3c20-a3eb-5b9a9c76216e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A phantasm (an impression received through the senses) or the faculty of receiving or representing these impressions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4b8e484-e543-46b4-bd48-3c5ca5d16114",
                                                "sense_id": "870a5eab-2d75-391d-9a6a-07349ad8cec6",
                                                "text": "Phantasia, then, is the animal's awareness of some object or state of affairs, which may well prove to be an object of desire. [...] I am thirsty; I have (in the absence of the object) a phantasia of drink. [...] Phantasia can also be used to account for delusion in practical cases: \"Poor dog, he saw that as water (or as drink) when it was really ammonia solution.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c6866e1-cf9c-4cd6-aea6-295a454aa0c1",
                                                "sense_id": "870a5eab-2d75-391d-9a6a-07349ad8cec6",
                                                "text": "[T]he possibility of eating a piece of pie might be presented to you by your seeing it on the kitchen table. This stage is called phantasia, presentation or impression. Corresponding to a phantasia is a lekton, a proposition or sayable, for example, it is fitting for me to eat that piece of pie, which the agent entertains but does not necessarily endorse when she has a phantasia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6685dab6-61a2-4844-ae79-5047096e219f",
                                                "sense_id": "870a5eab-2d75-391d-9a6a-07349ad8cec6",
                                                "text": "Chrysippus called 'experience' the \"treasury of phantasias\", [...] According to Chrysippus, the phantasias burdened with appearances can be distinguished from the true ones by the mobilization of former groups of phantasias and by the operations with them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8e4eadb-b860-4800-b43a-c3be124732e2",
                                                "sense_id": "870a5eab-2d75-391d-9a6a-07349ad8cec6",
                                                "text": "Everything in the created world has to be understood not just an appearance or image—a phantasia, in [John Scotus] Eriugena's vocabulary—but as at the same time a divine revelation or manifestation, [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                        "entry_id": "de09c59b-8d55-3c20-a3eb-5b9a9c76216e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated spelling of fantasia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9077d7ca-28bd-4b02-9fa9-a40fb6d69b9c",
                                                "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                                "text": "The little Italian party, before alluded to, had collected around the piano. The white and plump fingers of the gay and black-eyed daughter of the Roman marchioness were tripping lightly up and down the octaves of the instrument, and her little tastefully arranged head was merrily dancing from side to side, keeping time to the half-improvised phantasia, which trickled like a wayward stream from her hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f4d8cec-a76d-4484-b259-cebe46e8bc03",
                                                "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                                "text": "She [Josepha Barbara Auernhammer] published subsequently many works of her own, (in all 63,) which, as well as her play, especially the extempore phantasias, were distinguished by much delicate feeling and a vivid imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2aff4530-3d12-4040-9b22-a4afb617ba10",
                                                "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                                "text": "It is, however, a ceremony of immense antiquity, and the chief civil festival of the year among the Arabs, who love nothing more dearly than a \"phantasia\" of this sort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70f5b940-a6b7-4820-8e90-404a01147d23",
                                                "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                                "text": "[The Warrior's Barrow (Kjæmpehøjen)] admirably conformed to his employers' National-Romantic aims. This is equally true of the four new plays with which [Henrik] Ibsen honoured his contract: St. John's Night) (Sancthansnatten, 1853), a phantasia having a good deal in common with [William] Shakespeare's Midsummer Night's Dream [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5c546e2-7395-485d-842e-0960db683012",
                                                "sense_id": "af6eda27-ce23-3360-86b0-5951c66e7ee5",
                                                "text": "These are the years in which she [Ellen Terry] begins to sign her letters in a phantasia of different names."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e5bc25c7-4d2a-40d2-8059-c067e9eedb42",
                        "source_entry_id": "69dd2fe7-e527-3b52-acc0-292154e85079",
                        "source_sense_description": "Psychique imaginaire qui a la structure d'un scénario soutenant la réalisation d'un désir",
                        "target_lang_word": "fantasy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fantasy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a14484c-61b7-3967-80ec-a75916bd7b21",
                                        "entry_id": "19d88710-af02-3672-a05b-c96c8b0b1dcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which comes from one's imagination."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77bbbae4-23b1-460f-b3c3-551541a69fc1",
                                                "sense_id": "5a14484c-61b7-3967-80ec-a75916bd7b21",
                                                "text": "Is not this something more than fantasy?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "702dbfb0-db70-4617-a044-ad8704ed49b0",
                                                "sense_id": "5a14484c-61b7-3967-80ec-a75916bd7b21",
                                                "text": "A thousand fantasies / Begin to throng into my memory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9d9f24e-c913-4986-a23c-3a03dd976974",
                                                "sense_id": "5a14484c-61b7-3967-80ec-a75916bd7b21",
                                                "text": "The whole position was so tremendous and so absolutely unearthly, that I believe it actually lulled our sense of terror, but to this hour I often see it in my dreams, and at its mere phantasy wake up covered with cold sweat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3fdc3e7-c890-4986-9f0b-e10e469923a6",
                                                "sense_id": "5a14484c-61b7-3967-80ec-a75916bd7b21",
                                                "text": "Try as hard as it can, empirical science cannot come up with a naturalistic explanation; it can only slip into fantasies that make scientists feel good because they are in harmony with their opinions, prejudices, and unconscious assumptions about the nature of reality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "633188e6-782c-31c6-8c9e-1b88d8b916ac",
                                        "entry_id": "19d88710-af02-3672-a05b-c96c8b0b1dcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The literary genre generally dealing with themes of magic and the supernatural, imaginary worlds and creatures, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90d6dff3-3854-36ff-891f-7f49f619a884",
                                        "entry_id": "19d88710-af02-3672-a05b-c96c8b0b1dcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fantastical design."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "355eb6d8-fd39-49c2-b794-74508672f94f",
                                                "sense_id": "90d6dff3-3854-36ff-891f-7f49f619a884",
                                                "text": "Embroidered with fantasies and flourishes of gold thread."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3379de8b-25b6-31fd-9b5f-776eef47a33b",
                                        "entry_id": "19d88710-af02-3672-a05b-c96c8b0b1dcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The drug gamma-hydroxybutyric acid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fantasy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3d94eb2-b3f7-3f70-aec0-80dd0dce4d2c",
                                        "entry_id": "fe24b9f7-e0eb-31c0-b952-46a187a50c58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To conceive (something) mentally; to imagine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d65fdc1-e973-342e-ade4-bc56a817bcfb",
                                        "entry_id": "fe24b9f7-e0eb-31c0-b952-46a187a50c58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fantasize about something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67ecf349-408b-4e03-8e23-78e18c27b143",
                                                "sense_id": "4d65fdc1-e973-342e-ade4-bc56a817bcfb",
                                                "text": "Perhaps I would be able to help him recapture the well-being and emotional closeness he fantasied his brother had experienced with his parents prior to his birth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1232902e-4745-3a30-9f14-4f42ac29b7db",
                                        "entry_id": "fe24b9f7-e0eb-31c0-b952-46a187a50c58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To conceive mentally; to imagine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e9a250a-8393-46b9-b399-9d7090dd437b",
                                                "sense_id": "1232902e-4745-3a30-9f14-4f42ac29b7db",
                                                "text": "Firſt I phantaſied that if I liſt to take vpon me the crowne and imperiall Scepter of the realme, now was the time propice and conuenient."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74e67f66-ee4f-3bec-932b-870751f7b547",
                                        "entry_id": "fe24b9f7-e0eb-31c0-b952-46a187a50c58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have a fancy for; to be pleased with; to like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca19f5b0-7ab9-49d0-a83a-8b93af354eb6",
                                                "sense_id": "74e67f66-ee4f-3bec-932b-870751f7b547",
                                                "text": "Which he doth most fantasy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d2c1f8d-6cf4-4956-bf39-2f98f9b34b32",
                                                "sense_id": "74e67f66-ee4f-3bec-932b-870751f7b547",
                                                "text": "The kyng fantasied so much his daughter Anne that almost everything began to grow out of frame and good order"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
